( I sent this as a mail to Samuli Takala, the author of NHSOUND,
  but it may also be of interest to other hackers )

Hi!

Last weekend I fetched your NHSOUND1.ZIP from wuarchive. Thank you very
much for your efforts to bring sounds to NetHack.

I have an old SoundBlaster Version 1.5. When I first tried to run
NHSOUND, I got an error message "Error initialising card" (or similar).
But then I replaced CT-VOICE.DRV with the old one that was delivered
with my card, and then, NHSOUND worked fine.
(Though I'm going to change some of the sounds to fit them more to my
liking.)

Btw, I know that the Amiga and Mac version already come with sounds.
Maybe it's possible to port/enhance this sound routines to the DOS version.
Then the EMS hooks could be spared, and the versions were somewhat 
more compatible.

Greetings,
Matthias


